From 7180ea3669717589b43752ecb0229ff8bfcd6176 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lutfil Hadi <lutfilhadi1999@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 21:03:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7615: add experimental explicit TX beamforming

mt7615 has never advertised or enabled VHT TX beamforming, although the
hardware and firmware support it (MediaTek's vendor mt7615 driver ships
with eBF on). Add SU explicit beamformer support behind a new txbf
module parameter, off by default.

The firmware interface follows the vendor mt7615d driver:
- init: TXBF_ACTION sounding on in BF_PROCESSING mode, then
  BF_HW_ENABLE_STATUS_UPDATE with eBF enabled
- per station: the 36 byte MT7615 STA_REC_BF layout (shorter than the
  connac one) with PFMU 0xffff so firmware allocates the profile, the
  WTBL_BF ebf_vht bit and BF_DATA_PACKET_APPLY
- per station SU periodic sounding (txbf_snd_ms, default 100ms). The
  vendor driver relies on firmware rate control to trigger sounding,
  but mt76 does rate control on the host, so without this the firmware
  never sounds and no frame is beamformed.

The beamformer capability is reapplied once the EEPROM chainmask is
known, since mt7615_init_device() runs before mt7615_eeprom_init().

Add debugfs counters txbf_txs_{all,ebf,ibf} from the TX status E/I_TXBF
bits to verify it on air.

Tested on Xiaomi Redmi AC2100 (MT7621 + MT7615N 4x4) with ImmortalWrt
25.12.2 and N9 firmware 20200814: 97% of TX status reports to a VHT
SU beamformee carried E_TXBF (126730 of 130396), with TX retries going
from 9% to 4%.

Signed-off-by: Lutfil Hadi <lutfilhadi1999@gmail.com>
